tated as\n\n$$\nM∨(M∧N)≡M.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is *not* logically equivalent to $M.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\n- Statement II is logically equivalent to $M.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(M∧N)∨M & ≡M∨(M∧N) \\\\  & ≡M.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is logically equivalent to $M.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M∨(N∧M) & ≡M∨(M∧N) \\\\  & ≡M.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}]}
